From db8c3ee8e8b831e0ef99ab122ede79ab14775c2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayesh Rathod <jayesh4.rathod@ril.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 12:37:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] Add shared Pre-Scan Tradeability Gateway and corporate
 lifecycle registry

Steps 1-3 of the Cross-Scanner Eligibility and Corporate Lifecycle Sprint.

Problem
-------
JBCHEPHARM was amalgamated into TORNTPHARM (effective 2026-07-08, last traded
2026-07-16) yet kept appearing in Hull output a month later at its stale
2026-07-16 close of Rs 2,408.90. Every existing control failed open:

  * no symbol_master_v2 row  -> series defaulted to EQ, active check skipped
  * no corporate_actions_v3 row -> the +/-5/+14-day ex-date window found nothing
  * ~380 stale bars -> satisfied min_sessions in both V3 (260) and Pine (300)

This is a data-governance defect, not a strategy defect, so it is fixed at the
shared data layer rather than by blacklisting one ticker.

Added
-----
* v2/security_lifecycle.py - dated registry of terminal corporate events with
  successor symbols and exchange ratios. terminal_from is derived from
  last_trading_date + 1 so historical replays remain exact.
* v2/tradeability.py - the gateway. Eight mandatory rules, ten reason codes,
  per-symbol price freshness measured in sessions rather than calendar days.
  Fails closed on missing metadata. Strategy-agnostic, so V3, the Momentum
  Ladder, Hull Pine and Penny Shadow can share it without merging their logic.
* migrations/v2/005_security_lifecycle.sql plus the same DDL in
  ensure_v3_schema(), because this repo has no ordered migration runner.
* corporate_data/normalized/security_lifecycle_events.csv - the JBCHEPHARM
  record, git-backed for disposable CI runners.
* tests/test_tradeability_gateway.py - 39 tests.

Changed
-------
* v2/database.py - load_lifecycle_registry() (seeds from the CSV snapshot when
  the table is empty, so a runner that restored only prices is still safe),
  save_tradeability_audit(), and load_symbol_master() no longer drops
  delisting_date.
* nse_corporate_store.py - git-back the lifecycle CSV; skip absent tables
  instead of emitting a zero-column INSERT.

Historical data is untouched. Terminal marking is per market date, so a replay
of 2026-07-10 still admits JBCHEPHARM exactly as it was validly admitted then.

Verified against the real CSV store on market date 2026-08-20 (2,965 symbols):
JBCHEPHARM rejected as TERMINAL_MERGER with successor TORNTPHARM; TORNTPHARM
itself still tradeable; 2,127 eligible. Of the 838 rejections, all 343
fresh-but-unmastered symbols were confirmed to be ETFs and index funds, so no
genuine equity is lost. The 7 pre-existing Telegram copy-text failures in
tests/ are unchanged from main.

No wiring into V3, Momentum Ladder or Hull Pine yet; that is steps 4-6.
